Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  
(only tables that help answer the mid‑June sales question are listed)

• cleaned_weekly_sales.week_date : exact Monday‐of‑week date, lets us eyeball which rows sit around 15 June.  
• cleaned_weekly_sales.calendar_year : filter to 2018, 2019, 2020.  
• cleaned_weekly_sales.week_number : pick “four weeks before” (≈ weeks 20‑23) and “four weeks after” (≈ weeks 25‑28).  
• cleaned_weekly_sales.month_number : quick sanity‑check that chosen weeks really fall in May/June/July.  
• cleaned_weekly_sales.sales : metric we will aggregate and compare.  

Typical filter conditions we will need  
calendar_year IN (2018, 2019, 2020)  
AND week_number BETWEEN 20 AND 28               -- 9‑week window around 15 June  
AND week_number BETWEEN 20 AND 23               -- 4 weeks before 15 June  
AND week_number BETWEEN 25 AND 28               -- 4 weeks after 15 June  

Below are ten exploratory→analytic queries (all plain SELECTs, each limited to 20 rows).  
Double‑quotes are used around table / column names; every query is preceded by a short comment.

```sql
-- 1. Distinct calendar years present in the cleaned weekly‑sales table
SELECT DISTINCT "calendar_year"
FROM "cleaned_weekly_sales"
ORDER BY "calendar_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Which week numbers fall in June 2020?  (Quick check around mid‑June)
SELECT DISTINCT "week_number", "week_date"
FROM "cleaned_weekly_sales"
WHERE "calendar_year" = 2020
  AND "month_number" = 6
ORDER BY "week_number"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Raw weekly sales and dates for the 2018 nine‑week window (wk 20‑28)
SELECT "calendar_year", "week_number", "week_date", "sales"
FROM "cleaned_weekly_sales"
WHERE "calendar_year" = 2018
  AND "week_number" BETWEEN 20 AND 28
ORDER BY "week_number"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Aggregate total sales: 4 weeks BEFORE 15 June 2018 (wk 20‑23)
SELECT "calendar_year",
       SUM("sales") AS "pre_jun15_sales"
FROM "cleaned_weekly_sales"
WHERE "calendar_year" = 2018
  AND "week_number" BETWEEN 20 AND 23
GROUP BY "calendar_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Aggregate total sales: 4 weeks AFTER 15 June 2018 (wk 25‑28)
SELECT "calendar_year",
       SUM("sales") AS "post_jun15_sales"
FROM "cleaned_weekly_sales"
WHERE "calendar_year" = 2018
  AND "week_number" BETWEEN 25 AND 28
GROUP BY "calendar_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. 4‑week‑BEFORE totals for ALL target years, side‑by‑side
SELECT "calendar_year",
       SUM("sales") AS "pre_jun15_sales"
FROM "cleaned_weekly_sales"
WHERE "calendar_year" IN (2018, 2019, 2020)
  AND "week_number" BETWEEN 20 AND 23
GROUP BY "calendar_year"
ORDER BY "calendar_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. 4‑week‑AFTER totals for ALL target years, side‑by‑side
SELECT "calendar_year",
       SUM("sales") AS "post_jun15_sales"
FROM "cleaned_weekly_sales"
WHERE "calendar_year" IN (2018, 2019, 2020)
  AND "week_number" BETWEEN 25 AND 28
GROUP BY "calendar_year"
ORDER BY "calendar_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Combine BEFORE and AFTER aggregates for every year (no % yet)
WITH pre AS (
  SELECT "calendar_year", SUM("sales") AS pre_sales
  FROM   "cleaned_weekly_sales"
  WHERE  "calendar_year" IN (2018, 2019, 2020)
     AND "week_number" BETWEEN 20 AND 23
  GROUP  BY "calendar_year"
),
post AS (
  SELECT "calendar_year", SUM("sales") AS post_sales
  FROM   "cleaned_weekly_sales"
  WHERE  "calendar_year" IN (2018, 2019, 2020)
     AND "week_number" BETWEEN 25 AND 28
  GROUP  BY "calendar_year"
)
SELECT pre."calendar_year", pre.pre_sales, post.post_sales
FROM   pre
JOIN   post USING ("calendar_year")
ORDER  BY pre."calendar_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Calculate percentage change (post vs. pre) for each year
WITH pre AS (
  SELECT "calendar_year", SUM("sales") AS pre_sales
  FROM   "cleaned_weekly_sales"
  WHERE  "calendar_year" IN (2018, 2019, 2020)
     AND "week_number" BETWEEN 20 AND 23
  GROUP  BY "calendar_year"
),
post AS (
  SELECT "calendar_year", SUM("sales") AS post_sales
  FROM   "cleaned_weekly_sales"
  WHERE  "calendar_year" IN (2018, 2019, 2020)
     AND "week_number" BETWEEN 25 AND 28
  GROUP  BY "calendar_year"
)
SELECT pre."calendar_year",
       ROUND(100.0 * (post.post_sales - pre.pre_sales) / pre.pre_sales, 2) 
         AS "pct_change_post_vs_pre"
FROM   pre
JOIN   post USING ("calendar_year")
ORDER  BY pre."calendar_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Same %‑change query, but showing region‑level breakdown as well
WITH pre AS (
  SELECT "calendar_year", "region", SUM("sales") AS pre_sales
  FROM   "cleaned_weekly_sales"
  WHERE  "calendar_year" IN (2018, 2019, 2020)
     AND "week_number" BETWEEN 20 AND 23
  GROUP  BY "calendar_year", "region"
),
post AS (
  SELECT "calendar_year", "region", SUM("sales") AS post_sales
  FROM   "cleaned_weekly_sales"
  WHERE  "calendar_year" IN (2018, 2019, 2020)
     AND "week_number" BETWEEN 25 AND 28
  GROUP  BY "calendar_year", "region"
)
SELECT pre."calendar_year", pre."region",
       ROUND(100.0 * (post.post_sales - pre.pre_sales) / pre.pre_sales, 2) 
         AS "pct_change_post_vs_pre"
FROM   pre
JOIN   post USING ("calendar_year", "region")
ORDER  BY pre."calendar_year", pre."region"
LIMIT 20;
```

